  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GOVERNING MEASUREMENT. docs/measurements/0001-taint-flow-precision.md puts taint-flow precision at ~41% population-weighted across six real repositories. Per WI-sivuz's PRE-REGISTERED decision bands -- named before any interval was computed, so the interval cannot be used to move them -- that is the <50% band: \"precision is the headline problem and recall work should stop until it is understood.\"\n\nP1 -> P2. This item is NAMED IN THE MEASUREMENT, in consequence 1: \"Fixes that make more sinks matchable (INV-suril, INV-gijis) will add flows at roughly this precision unless the flows they add are DDG-confirmed. An argument for sequencing, not for abandoning them.\" This is that sequencing, applied. It was at rank 10 while the precision mechanisms the same document names sat at ranks 75-76.\n\nTHE DEFECT IS UNCHANGED and re-reproduced at tip 2026-08-17: Files.write and Files.readAllBytes emit with call_construct=None while File.exists and File.mkdirs emit cc=method in the SAME run."  # 51a7
- op: discuss  # 0367
  at: '2026-08-25T04:13:58Z'  # 0367
  by: agent  # 0367
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0367
  clock: 6  # 0367
  nonce: '0367'  # 0367
  message: "PHASE 0 RE-VERIFICATION AT TIP, 2026-08-25, dev e41a655d6d. THE CAUSE HAS\nMOVED. The statement still fails, but not for the reason filed.\n\nFiles.write(p, b) at tip emits cc=method with module_hint java.nio.file.Files\n(WI-sajis PR #498 landed the stamp), so the catalogue kind:method is no longer\nthe blocker. The blocker is now the NAME:\n\n    lookup_with_module('Files.write', 'java.nio.file.Files') -> None\n    lookup_with_module('write',       'java.nio.file.Files') -> IoPrimitive(fs_write, ...)\n\nThe java analyzer emits the callee name WITH its receiver prefix; the\ncatalogue keys on the bare method name. The whole 22-entry\njava.nio.file.Files surface is still unmatchable, by a different mechanism.\n\nSAME ROOT AS WI-nakut's JAVA HALF (receiver prefix u.mkdirs cannot match\njava.io.File.mkdirs). One root cause, two items -- fix once, at the producer\nor at the lookup, not twice.\n\nRE-CLASSIFIED FOR THE CAMPAIGN: this is a MISS (recall), not a false clean, so\nit sits in Phase 6 behind the band ruling, not Phase 1. Status unchanged:\nviolated."  # 0367
- op: update  # dcac
  at: '2026-09-07T22:51:11Z'  # dcac
  by: agent  # dcac
  actor: jgstern_agent  # dcac
  clock: 7  # dcac
  nonce: dcac  # dcac
  set:  # dcac
    title: "java.lang statics carry no module slot unless the file happens to have a wildcard import, so the implicitly-imported catalogue surface (env_read sources, subprocess sinks) is unreachable"  # dcac
    fields:  # dcac
      statement: "A java call site's module slot must carry the owner path THE LANGUAGE PUTS IN\nSCOPE, not only the paths the file happens to spell. A catalogued I/O primitive\non a java.lang class -- implicitly imported in every compilation unit under\nJLS 7.3 -- must be reachable from a call site that writes no import for it,\nbecause none is required and no java source does.\n\nSUPERSEDES two earlier statements of this invariant, both refuted at tip and\nquoted here so the supersession is legible rather than silent:\n\n  (1) AS FILED 2026-08-10: \"A catalogued I/O primitive whose call construct\n      differs from the analyzer's emitted construct can never be tagged;\n      static-method entries must be catalogued as the construct the AST\n      actually produces.\" REFUTED: the construct is no longer the blocker\n      (WI-sajis PR #498 stamps cc=method on the static call), and the\n      prescribed remedy -- re-keying static entries as `functions:` -- is not\n      what fixed it and would not have. A file using `import static\n      java.nio.file.Files.write;` emits cc=None on a method-kind entry AND\n      CLASSIFIES ANYWAY, because the module-hint path never consults the\n      construct. The construct clause was the wrong mechanism from the start.\n\n  (2) AS RE-MECHANISED 2026-08-25: \"the java analyzer emits the callee name\n      WITH its receiver prefix; the catalogue keys on the bare method name.\n      The whole 22-entry java.nio.file.Files surface is still unmatchable.\"\n      REFUTED: `strip_redundant_module_qualifier` (INV-januj / INV-fofoj)\n      strips a head the module slot already carries, so `java.nio.file.Files`\n      + `Files.write` composes to `write` and matches. The prefix is only\n      fatal when the module slot is a PLACEHOLDER, which is what clause (1)\n      of this statement now names.\n\nWHAT SURVIVED BOTH REFUTATIONS is the invariant's original subject -- a\ncatalogued primitive that no call site can reach -- and its live population is\njava.lang, the one package a correct java file never imports."  # dcac
- op: update  # a3ca
  at: '2026-09-07T22:51:11Z'  # a3ca
  by: agent  # a3ca
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a3ca
  clock: 8  # a3ca
  nonce: a3ca  # a3ca
  set:  # a3ca
    fields:  # a3ca
      root_cause: "The java analyzer's capitalised-static-receiver branch resolved a receiver\nthrough explicit imports, or (since INV-hahak) through a wildcard import, and\nwas gated on `wildcard_imports` being non-empty. A file with only single-type\nimports -- the style every java linter enforces -- took no branch at all, so\nthe module slot stayed `external`.\n\nThe two failures then COMPOUND rather than merely coexist: with a placeholder\nin the module slot, `strip_redundant_module_qualifier` refuses to fire (its\nfirst guard is exactly that placeholder set), so the callee also keeps its\n`System.` prefix. The catalogue's bare-name key is therefore unreachable from\nboth directions in the same edge -- no module to filter on, and a name that is\nnot the row's name.\n\nFIXED by extending the branch gate to `(wildcard_imports or receiver_name in\n_JAVA_LANG_TYPES)`, the closed JLS 7.3 list the analyzer already carried;\n`_wildcard_candidate_slot([], \"System\")` yields exactly `java.lang.System`."  # a3ca
- op: discuss  # 17d7
  at: '2026-09-07T22:51:11Z'  # 17d7
  by: agent  # 17d7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 17d7
  clock: 9  # 17d7
  nonce: 17d7  # 17d7
  message: "RE-SCOPED AND SATISFIED ON A REWRITTEN STATEMENT, 2026-09-07, measurement 0017.\nSame pattern as INV-gijis two days ago: rewrite the clause the gate actually\nneeds, QUOTE the superseded text, then close on the rewritten one.\n\nBOTH OF THIS ITEM'S EARLIER MECHANISMS ARE DEAD AT TIP, verified through the\nPRODUCTION analyzer and the PRODUCTION classify_call before anything was built\n(suril_09072026/probe.py, probe2.py):\n  - THE CONSTRUCT CLAUSE (as filed): a file using `import static\n    java.nio.file.Files.write;` emits cc=None on a method-KIND entry AND\n    CLASSIFIES ANYWAY, because the module-hint path never consults the\n    construct. The filing's prescribed remedy -- re-key static entries as\n    `functions:` -- is not what fixed it and would not have.\n  - THE NAME CLAUSE (2026-08-25): `strip_redundant_module_qualifier`\n    (INV-januj / INV-fofoj) strips a head the module slot already carries, so\n    `java.nio.file.Files` + `Files.write` composes to `write` and matches.\n  - THE FILED REPRO NO LONGER REPRODUCES. sherpa-onnx's\n    `java:java.nio.file.Files:0-0:copy` and `createTempDirectory` -- the two\n    dsts this item names -- are that repository's ONLY two Files.* edges and\n    BOTH classify at tip. The item's own population is clean.\n\nWHAT SURVIVED IS THE SUBJECT, NOT EITHER MECHANISM: a catalogued primitive no\ncall site can reach. Its live population is `java.lang`, the one package a\ncorrect java file never imports. Statement and root_cause rewritten to that,\nwith the two superseded texts quoted in the statement itself.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, and the two failures COMPOUND rather than coexist: the\ncapitalised-static-receiver branch was gated on `wildcard_imports` being\nnon-empty (INV-hahak built it for wildcard files), so a file with only\nsingle-type imports took NO branch and kept `external`. With a placeholder in\nthe module slot `strip_redundant_module_qualifier` also refuses to fire -- its\nfirst guard is exactly that placeholder set -- so the name keeps its `System.`\nprefix too. Unreachable from both directions in one edge.\n\nFIXED by admitting any name in the closed JLS 7.3 `_JAVA_LANG_TYPES` list the\nanalyzer already carried. A project-class guard was written and REMOVED as\nunreachable: `class_resolver` claims a project class name first and emits a\nRESOLVED edge (verified on two fixtures -- the class in the calling package and\nin a different one), and in the second case the guard would also have been\nWRONG, since `app.P` calling `System.currentTimeMillis()` without importing\n`other.System` means java.lang's by JLS 6.5.\n\nSIZED BEFORE, MEASURED AFTER (0017, three java repositories, both arms\nasserting their java.py BLOB because both trees were dirty and a commit sha\nwould not describe the bytes):\n  cassandra   459 edges lost pre-fix, against 446 java calls that classify in\n              the ENTIRE repository. 15 of 142 java rows (10.6%) are java.lang.\n  delta       21 situations added, 0 LOST, 0 WRONG-TYPE of 21; RC1 (a repo\n              defining System/Runtime/ProcessBuilder itself) and RC2 (a matched\n              row outside java.lang.*) both EMPTY on all three repos.\n  precision   2 certain TP (9.5%), 3 counting one plausible (14.3%).\n\nTHE PRECISION FIGURE IS DISCLOSED AS A FLOOR AND THE REASON IS FILED. java has\nno def/use extractor (WI-gotun, open; the run's own dataflow_coverage reports\njava dataflow_capable=false). Every java flow is structural / walk=unavailable,\nso the 3a walk refutes none of them, and all 18 false positives are the shape a\nwalk removes. It ships rather than being withheld the WI-sihoh way because the\nBASELINE's own java findings are 3 of 3 in the SAME regime -- this scales java's\nexisting precision, it does not introduce a worse one -- and because eight\nblindness caveats (untyped_receiver, unknown_receiver_scope,\nanalyzer_construct_blind, analyzer_method_call_blind) RETIRE on jenkins\nindependent of any walk.\n\nREPORTED BECAUSE NOTHING MOVED THERE: cassandra gained 273 structural findings\nand ZERO claim violations -- the additions are dominated by currentTimeMillis /\nnanoTime, which mint host_description, and the claim set has no\nhost-description-no-logging and no host-description-no-host-fs. 273 findings\nlanding outside the seven questions asked is not \"the fix did nothing\".\n\nFAMILY SWEPT AND FILED, NOT CHASED (LIVE rule 4): kotlin 22 of 186 catalogue\nrows and scala 57 of 184 live on auto-imported modules, both confirmed on\nemission with a control. Their shape DIFFERS -- kotlin and scala drop the\nreceiver entirely and emit the bare method -- so java's fix does not transfer.\nFiled as its own item; kotlin.py's now-false docstring claim that such a list\n\"buys nothing yet\" is corrected in this PR."  # 17d7
